# Start: turns_king_tax_accept's input.sav (France, turn 108; England at peace, the Europe-bound Caravel held at
# sea, French units fortified) with the calendar moved to Autumn 1799 (head.year 1799, autumn 1).
# End of turn 108 reaches Spring 1800: the peacetime calendar end, FUN_3844_0442 raw 58629-58676
# (`!(0x5382 & 0x10)`, year 0x708 = 1800, no WoI): @RETIRING ("Viceroy Jacques Cartier steps down ...",
# estate = the most populous French colony, last of ties: Montreal), the retire chain without the @RETIRE
# confirm (F10 score report, exploits screen, Hall of Fame), then @SCORED; "Keep playing anyway." (row 1)
# returns to the map with calendar_latch (0x5382 |= 0x10) set. The empty Hall of Fame file is written too.
# Turn 109 (Spring 1800 to Autumn 1800) plays on: the calendar block is off, nothing re-fires; the King's tax
# raise is accepted (@TAXOPTIONS row 0), as in turns_king_tax_accept.
key space                # end turn 108 (Autumn 1799)
wait 30
key Return               # SoL in Quebec up to 60%: Continue turn
wait 10
key Return               # @RETIRING: Viceroy Jacques Cartier steps down (estate near Montreal)
wait 10
key Return               # F10 score report
wait 10
key Return               # exploits screen
wait 10
key Return               # Hall of Fame
wait 10
key Return               # price of Cigars rises
wait 10
key Down                 # @SCORED: bar to row 1
key Return               # "Keep playing anyway.": main map
wait 10
shot                     # Spring 1800: End of Turn
key space                # end turn 109
wait 30
key Return               # Iroquois gift of 16 Ore to Port au Prince
wait 6
                         # King raises tax by 1% to 27% (@KINGTAX)
key Return               # @TAXOPTIONS row 0: Kiss pinky ring
wait 6
key Return               # SoL in Port au Prince 12%: Continue turn
wait 6
key Return               # SoL in Martinique 51%: Continue turn
wait 6
key Return               # SoL in Guadeloupe 70%: Continue turn
wait 6
key Return               # Horses cargo ready at Montreal: Continue turn
wait 6
key Return               # @TRAINPROFESSION: a colonist in Quebec has learned Fisherman
wait 10
shot                     # Autumn 1800: End of Turn, no second @RETIRING
